\p
\v 14 Then¦49149 \add @Yeshua¦49150\add* drove out¦49151 a¦49152 demon¦49152 that caused muteness, and¦49160 after the¦49161 demon¦49162 departed, the¦49168 man¦49169 was able to speak¦49167. The¦49174 crowds¦49175 were amazed¦49172,
\v 15 but¦49178 yet some¦49177 of¦49179 them¦49180 said¦49183, “He's¦49192 driving¦49192 out¦49192 demons¦49195 because he's Beelzebul the¦49187 leader¦49189 of¦49190 the¦49190 demons¦49191.”\x + \xo 11:15: \xt Mat 9:34; 10:25.\x*
\p
\v 16 Others¦49206 who wanted¦49216 to test¦49208 \add who he was\add*, asked \add @Yeshua\add* to send a¦49209 sign¦49209 from¦49214 heaven,\x + \xo 11:16: \xt Mrk 8:11; Mat 12:38; 16:1.\x*
\v 17 but¦49220 he¦49219 knew¦49221 their¦49222 thoughts¦49224 and told¦49226 them¦49227, “\wj Any kingdom¦49229 that's divided¦49235 against¦49232 itself¦49233 is¦49236 doomed, and¦49237 any household that's divided will self-destruct.\wj*
\v 18 \wj \+add ≈So¦49244\+add* if¦49243 Satan¦49247 was¦49252 fighting against¦49248 himself¦49249, how¦49254 could his¦49258 kingdom¦49257 even remain? Yes, I know that you're¦49261 all¦49261 saying¦49261 that I must be Beelzebul in order to¦49265 drive out¦49265 demons¦49270,\wj*
\v 19 \wj but¦49272 if¦49271 I¦49273 have Beelzebul's power over demons¦49278, then whose power do \+em your¦49281\+em* apprentices use to drive out¦49286 demons?\wj*
\v 20 \wj However if¦49299 I'm¦49305 driving¦49306 out¦49306 demons¦49308 with \+add ≈power\+add* that comes¦49310 from God, then that means that \nd God's¦49304\nd* kingdom¦49314 is right in the middle \+nd of\+nd* you¦49312 all¦49312.\wj*
\p
\v 21 “\wj Whenever¦49317 a strong¦49319 \+add landowner\+add* arms¦49320 himself¦49325 and guards¦49322 his¦49334 nice home, everything remains there peacefully¦49329,\wj*
\v 22 \wj but¦49337 when¦49336 someone stronger¦49339 than¦49339 him¦49340 arrives¦49342 and overpowers¦49345 him¦49347, he'll¦49351 even take¦49351 the¦49348 body armour¦49349 that¦49353 the \+add landowner\+add* \+add ≈put his¦49350 trust¦49354 in¦49352\+add*, and¦49356 then relieve him of all his¦49359 goods.\wj*
\p
\v 23 “\wj Anyone who doesn't \+add follow\+add* me¦49367 is¦49370 against¦49368 me¦49369, and¦49371 anyone who doesn't gather¦49374 with¦49375 us, \+add wants to\+add* scatter¦49377 us.\wj*\x + \xo 11:23: \xt Mrk 9:40.\x*
