\p
\v 24 “\wj Whenever¦49379 an evil spirit¦49383 leaves a person¦49387, it¦49388 roams through inhospitable places¦49393 \+add ≈looking¦49394 for¦49394\+add* \+add somewhere to\+add* rest¦49395, and¦49396 when it doesn't find¦49398 \+add a home\+add*, it¦49402 says¦49402, ‘\+add Ah,\+add* I'll¦49403 return¦49403 to¦49404 the¦49405 home¦49406 that I¦49409 \+add recently\+add* left¦49409.’\wj*
\v 25 \wj Then when it¦49413 gets back there, it¦49413 finds¦49413 the home swept¦49415 out and¦49416 tidied up,\wj*
\v 26 \wj so it¦49419 goes¦49419 and¦49420 finds seven¦49430 other¦49426 spirits¦49427 more¦49428 evil¦49428 than¦49428 itself¦49429. They all move in and live¦49434 there¦49435, so¦49436 the result is that¦49442 the person¦49441 ends up worse¦49443 in the end¦49439 than¦49443 \+add they were\+add* at the¦49444 beginning.\wj*”
